    {
      "id": 7,
      "user": "employee",
      "question": "What's the process to onboard a new vendor and who approves over $10k?",
      "expected_outcome": "answer",
      "expected_source": [
        "finance_vendor_onboarding.md",
        "procurement_approval_matrix.md"
      ],
      "actual_outcome": "answer",
      "answer": "Onboarding process (applies to any new vendor expected to receive payment): 1) The business owner submits a New Vendor Request in the procurement portal with business justification and estimated annual spend. 2) The vendor provides a W-9 (or W-8 for non-U.S. vendors), certificate of insurance, and banking details. 3) A security review via IT Security is required if the vendor will access company systems or handle company or customer data. 4) Approval, based on spend per the Procurement Approval Matrix. 5) Accounts Payable creates the vendor record after approval and verifies bank details by call-back to a known phone number. 6) A purchase order is issued before work begins for any spend over $2,500.\n\nApprovers over $10k (based on total contract value, or annual spend for recurring contracts): $10,001-$50,000 requires the Department head plus the Finance Director; $50,001-$250,000 requires the VP of Finance plus the COO; over $250,000 requires the CFO plus the CEO. Additionally, sole-source purchases over $10,000 require a written justification, and contracts with auto-renewal clauses require Legal review regardless of value.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "finance_vendor_onboarding.md",
          "section": "1. When this applies"
        },
        {
          "source": "finance_vendor_onboarding.md",
